#14504
A dead end~
No sooner than you enter the dead end of the corridor than you feel a sudden
queasy sensation in the pit of your stomach. A kaleidoscope of images flashes
before you, then you are struck by buffeting winds, but they subside before
they do more than ruffle your hair. It would appear you are now some where 
else. Taking in your surroundings, you note a fine grey mist hanging in the 
air. The light filtering through the mist seems quite dim, then you realise it 
is the mist itself that emits the light. The walls here are of rough stone,
covered in slick slime. You note there are scratches and gouges in the stone 
here.
~
145 72 0 0 0 0 255 0
D0
