#14516
A misty tunnel~
As soon as you enter the tunnel you experience a queasy feeling in the pit of
your stomach and are struck by buffeting winds which subside almost as soon as
they begin. Recovering from the sudden disorientation, you find yourself some
where else. Taking in your new surroundings, you find your self in a room of
grey stone. To your north, south, east and west simple archways lead to stone
corridors. Torches above the arches provide light. At least there is none of 
the mist here.
~
