#14551
A Misty Cavern~
The misty tunnels widen here into a small cavern. The fine mist hanging in the
air makes it difficult to see a great deal of detail. Puddles filling 
depressions in the cavern floor could be just a few inches deep, or could be 
deep holes, waiting to take you to a watery grave. Wisely, you step around 
them. The small cavern extends to the south and east. To the north, a passage
skirts around a immense rock formation to the west.
~
